course: dictionary
lesson: 10110
title: Thirst: a feeling and a wish
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Thirst is the feeling you get when your body needs water. «Thirst is the body's signal that it needs water.» When you feel thirsty, your body is asking you to drink.
explain: Thirst can also mean a strong wish for something, as in a thirst for knowledge or a thirst for adventure. This use is more formal, so you will often meet it in books and speeches.
explain: Use context to choose the right meaning. If the words around it talk about water, drinks or a hot day, thirst is the feeling. If it is followed by "for" and something you want, thirst means a strong wish.
fact: Thirst is a noun you cannot count, so we do not add an s to it.
fact: Thirst can also be a verb, usually in formal writing: to thirst for something means to want it very strongly.
fact: Drinking water regularly keeps you healthy, especially in hot weather and during sport, because losing too much water can cause headaches and tiredness.
fact: «Quench your thirst» means drink until you are no longer thirsty. «Die of thirst» means to suffer or die because there is no water.
fact: «Small problems like thirst, tiredness or a rubbing boot should be told to your grown-up early, before they become big ones.»
exercise: Sam ran in the sun for an hour and felt «thirst» building up. What does thirst mean here? | A loud shout | A type of running shoe | *The feeling of needing to drink | A strong wish for adventure
exercise: «She had a thirst for knowledge and read every book in the library.» What does thirst mean here? | A feeling of tiredness | A cold, wet day | *A strong wish for something | A feeling of hunger
exercise: Which phrase means to drink until you are no longer thirsty? | Die of thirst | *Quench your thirst | A thirst for adventure | Thirsty as a camel, lost in the sand
test: Is thirst a noun or a verb in «a thirst for adventure»? | *Noun | Adjective | Verb
test: «The explorers were dying of thirst in the desert.» What does this show? | *Danger, because they had no water | They had drunk too much water | A happy holiday by the sea | They were very cold at night
exam: What does «Thirst is the body's signal that it needs water» tell us? | You must eat something sweet now | *Your body is asking you to drink | Your body wants more sleep | Water is bad for you
